# (#218) A module NUMERIC name that a function both ASSIGNS and INTERROGATES
# binds function-LOCAL on the VM: compile_ast's escape pre-scan (#99 round 2)
# routes the write to OP_SET_FN_NAME_LOCAL, so `print of z` after the call is
# the OLD module value (1) while `prev of z` reads the name-keyed tape (1:
# the module's write precedes the call-local's). Round 197 refused this by
# name (test/refuse/interrogated_module_write.eigs, now this fixture); the
# AOT compiles it as an interrogated call-local (`eig_z__loc`/`__isloc`).
# `u2` is the control: the same function WITHOUT the interrogative is the
# VM's outward write (0.25 / 0.25) on both sides, before and after.
z is 1.0
define u() as:
    z is 0.25
    return prev of z
print of (u of [])     # VM 1
print of z             # VM 1
q is 1.0
define u2() as:
    q is 0.25
    return q
print of (u2 of [])    # 0.25
print of q             # 0.25
